    "c1": {
      "anchor": "i35",
      "kind": "item",
      "label": "No words for paging by a Link header or an offset, a read-only web server, or what a server can filter and sort",
      "excerpt": "No words for paging by a Link header or an offset, a read-only web server, or what a server can filter and sort",
      "text": "some sites dont' use names limit and offset, make sure this works with other patterns",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-09T03:50:41.552Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-09T04:04:09.017Z",
          "html": "<p>\n  You were right: free names weren't enough. <code>\"per_page\" and \"page\"</code> would have asked for the wrong page, a\n  token could only go back as <code>cursor</code>, and a next link written as a path was sent as a cursor. Each shape\n  below now has a line and a test against a fake server, in English and Spanish.\n</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>A count and a position, any names: <code>its next page is asked for with \"take\" and \"skip\"</code>. Tested with <code>\"count\" and \"start\"</code>, <code>\"$top\" and \"$skip\"</code>, <code>\"rows\" and \"start\"</code>.</li>\n  <li>Only a position, its page size its own: <code>its next page is asked for with \"start\"</code>.</li>\n  <li>A page's number: <code>its next page is asked for by number with \"per_page\" and \"page\"</code>. Also <code>\"pageSize\" and \"pageNumber\"</code>.</li>\n  <li>A first page of 0: add <code>, counting from 0</code> to that line. Without it, 1.</li>\n  <li>Only a page's number: <code>its next page is asked for by number with \"p\"</code>.</li>\n  <li>A token in the answer, sent back under another name: <code>its next page is its \"nextPageToken\", sent back as \"pageToken\"</code>.</li>\n  <li>A cursor inside the answer, sent back as <code>cursor</code>: <code>its next page is the \"next_cursor\" of its \"meta\"</code> (already there).</li>\n  <li>A next page written in the answer, a whole address, a path or just <code>?at=2</code>: <code>its next page is its \"next\"</code> (paths are new).</li>\n  <li>A <code>Link</code> header: <code>its next page is in its \"Link\" header</code> (already there).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Names that would do the wrong thing no longer compile, and the message says what to write:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><code>asked for with \"per_page\" and \"page\"</code> counts pages, not rows.</li>\n  <li><code>asked for with \"limit\" and \"cursor\"</code>: a cursor comes from the answer.</li>\n  <li>The two names the wrong way round, as in <code>\"skip\" and \"take\"</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Two things to know:</p>\n<ol>\n  <li>\n    <b>Not covered: a server that wants the last row's id back, like Stripe's <code>starting_after</code> with\n    <code>has_more</code>.</b> No line says that, so a read of one gets its first page only.\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    A server told how many that gives fewer still needs <code>it gives up to 50 at a time</code>, or a read stops at its\n    first page. A server told only where from, with its size unsaid, is read until a page comes back empty: one request\n    more.\n  </li>\n</ol>\n<p>This is on the agent's branch, and will show once it's merged.</p>"
        },
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "at": "2026-11-09T04:19:47.936Z",
